{
  "id": "T-1747",
  "created_at": 1791527418.639056,
  "parent": "T-1745",
  "role": "review",
  "tier": "sonnet",
  "complexity": 7,
  "title": "review: Clear stale dispatched_at on queued tasks whose worker died (daemon restart), so they dispatch again",
  "spec": "Evidence (luna-inbox, 2026-10-09): T-0676 was dispatched at 06:48:39; the daemon restart at 06:49 (PR 48 deploy) killed\nits worker before it started work. The task stayed status=queued with pipeline.dispatched_at, dispatched_at_lease and\ndispatched_at_done set and no pid. orchestrator/daemon.py dispatch (around line 984) then skips it forever with reason \"other\"\nbecause it is not in the wave and has dispatched_at. It sat 70 min until the Planner cleared the stamps by hand. This has happened\nrepeatedly (T-0617, T-0618 and others on 2026-10-08).\nFix: on each tick (cheap, from the per-tick bus snapshot), a task with status queued, a dispatched_at stamp, and no live worker\n(no pid, or a pid that is not alive, and no worker_registry entry) for longer than [dispatch].stale_stamp_grace_s (default 120 s)\ngets its dispatched_at* stamps cleared and a one-line event \"stale dispatch stamp cleared (worker gone)\". Never touch a task with a\nlive worker or a running/held/done status. Also make the skip reason say \"stale_dispatch_stamp\" instead of \"other\" while the grace\nruns. Tests (tests/test_daemon.py): test_stale_dispatch_stamp_cleared_after_grace, test_live_worker_stamp_kept,\ntest_skip_reason_names_stale_stamp. Run: PYTHONPATH=tests uv run python -m unittest tests.test_daemon. Commit on the task branch.",
  "inputs": [
    "T-1746"
  ],
  "acceptance": [
    "queued tasks with a dead worker's dispatch stamp dispatch again after the grace",
    "live workers and non-queued tasks are untouched",
    "the three named tests pass",
    "tests.test_daemon passes"
  ],
  "scope": [
    "orchestrator/daemon.py",
    "orchestrator/pool.py",
    "tests/test_daemon.py",
    "docs/daemon.md"
  ],
  "depends_on": [],
  "constraints": {
    "read_only": true,
    "budget_turns": 20,
    "timeout_s": 900
  },
  "status": "done",
  "assigned_to": "claude:B",
  "worktree": "/Users/k3ntaw/code/orchestrator/wt/T-1747",
  "codex_thread": null,
  "result": {
    "summary": "The implementation matches the acceptance criteria. Only daemon.py and tests/test_daemon.py changed, and docs/daemon.md and pool.py were not touched. Stamps are cleared only for queued, non-goal execute tasks that have no live worker, after the grace period. A live worker is detected from an in-process dispatch thread, a live pid on the task, or a registry entry that is non-terminal and has no pid or a live one. The clear is re-checked under bus.locked() to avoid races. The skip reason is 'stale_dispatch_stamp' while a dead stamp is inside the grace window, and 'other' for live workers. The three named tests exist as unittest methods and cover clearing after the grace, keeping live and non-queued tasks, and the skip reason. I did not run the suite.",
    "verdict": "approve",
    "comments": [
      {
        "path": "orchestrator/daemon.py",
        "line": 857,
        "issue": "_dispatch_live only knows about dispatch threads in this process (_LIVE_DISPATCH), a live task pid, or a worker_registry entry. A worker started by a different process (daemon --once or a Planner-run pass) that has not yet written a registry entry or pid, such as a Codex MCP worker still in setup, would count as dead after 120s and be re-dispatched. The claim path probably sets status=running before this matters, so the exposure is small. I did not verify it.",
        "severity": "low"
      },
      {
        "path": "orchestrator/daemon.py",
        "line": 836,
        "issue": "The new [dispatch].stale_stamp_grace_s setting is not documented. docs/daemon.md is in scope but was not updated, and pool.py has no default. The default exists only as the STALE_STAMP_GRACE_S constant.",
        "severity": "low"
      },
      {
        "path": "orchestrator/daemon.py",
        "line": 857,
        "issue": "The clear logic requires `not pipeline.get('gated_at')`, which the spec does not mention. This is reasonable since a gated task is past dispatch, but no test covers it.",
        "severity": "low"
      }
    ],
    "packet_version": "7cbc35e09c20",
    "confidence": 0.0,
